            <ArticleTitle>Multifocal tuberculosis revealed by spinal tuberculosis in an eleven-year-old Guianese child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>234-237</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s13149-017-0570-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Multifocal tuberculosis in a child is rare event. Here we report a case of multifocal tuberculosis revealed by spinal tuberculosis in an eleven-year-old French Guianese girl. This observation underlines the difficulties, the consequences of delay, and the necessity of an early diagnosis of this disease for children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
